<title>USA: Sport Supply Q3 oper shr $0.06 vs $0.13.</title>
<headline>Sport Supply Q3 oper shr $0.06 vs $0.13.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Oper shr		    $0.06		    $0.13</p>
<p> Oper net			444			948</p>
<p> Revs			 21,920		   20,644</p>
<p> Avg shrs		    6,777		    7,023</p>
<p>			9   MONTHS</p>
<p> Oper shr		     0.07		     0.25</p>
<p> Oper net			448		    1,755</p>
<p> Revs			 60,657		   52,996</p>
<p> Avg shrs		    6,772		    6,928</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers) NOTE: The company said earnings for the three months ended August 2, 1996 exclude a non-cash charge of $0.55 per share associated with the planned disposition of its remaining golf assets. Earnings for the nine months ended August 2, 1996 exclude a $2.10 loss from discontinued operations.</p>
<p>Sport Supply also said it violated a single earnings related covenant in its loan agreement that will result in higher interest rates until it can halt the default through debt reduction or higher earnings.</p>
</text>
